  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A heater is used to supply energy to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> kg of water. The temperature of the water increases from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"250\"></span> K to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"252.4\"></span> K in two minutes. The power rating of the heater is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> watts. Assuming that no energy is lost during the process, what is the mass of the water?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{50P}{c}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{P}{50c}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50cP\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{50}{cP}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
